    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PAPERCLIP_DS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Seconds the OLDEST agent stuck in the session_unavailable bucket has continuously held status='error' (paperclip_agent_status_error_oldest_age_seconds). The red dashed line at 120s is BLO-18012's acceptance bound: 'time-to-recovery <= a small fixed window (target: <= 2 min), independent of that agent's heartbeat interval'. Crossing it is a real finding to report on BLO-18012, NOT something to retune this panel to hide.\n\nDELIBERATELY SCOPED TO session_unavailable. Charting every bucket here would drag in unrelated long-lived failures -- the 2581s BackoffLimitExceeded agent seen on 2026-09-10 would have sailed over the 2-min line and read as a BLO-18012 breach that never happened. The bound applies to this condition only.\n\nLower bound, never an overstatement: age derives from agents.updated_at, so an unrelated write to a still-errored row resets the clock. This series can under-report a breach; it cannot invent one. Reads 0 when nothing is wedged, and an empty panel means the exporter is down.",
